# Tandem public-release build output (scripts/release-tandem.js, ADR-0028)
dist/
# Generated demo dashboard rendered from the fixture during the build
demo-fixture/_00-Project-Management/42-Monitor/DASHBOARD.html

# The live board (ADR-0276, STORY-35.3.04). ~38 MB of fully-regenerable build output — run
# `npm run pm:dash` and it comes back; the Stop hook does it routinely. It was tracked for dev
# convenience and that convenience was expensive: 583 commits touched it, it is the Windows
# file-lock-during-merge hazard the phase merges have to use plumbing to work around, and it
# sat in the dev-install payload. ADR-0082 already gitignores this file in every CONSUMER
# install as "fully-regenerable build output"; this line applies the same stance to the repo
# that wrote the rule. NOTE: history is NOT rewritten — the existing blobs stay in the object
# store and the repo does not shrink. This stops the bleeding; it does not undo it.
# A fresh clone has no board until the first `npm run pm:dash`, which is the documented step.
_00-Project-Management/42-Monitor/DASHBOARD.html

# Tandem conversation-mode state — machine/session-local (joined session IDs)
.tandem-mode.json

# Playwright MCP scratch output
.playwright-mcp/

# Mutant sidecars written by the suite's positive controls. A dozen tests copy a LIVE script
# in 93-Scripts/ to `.mutant-<pid>-<seq>-<name>.js` (or `<name>.mutant-backup-<pid>-<seq>`),
# break it, prove the guard fires, then delete it. On the happy path nothing survives — but a
# timeout or a crash mid-mutant leaves a deliberately-BROKEN copy of a production script sitting
# untracked next to the real one, and an unscoped `git add -A` would commit it. Ignored so that
# cannot happen. (EPIC-30 phase-close review; the same run's own retro records the mutant harness
# corrupting generate-dashboard.js twice.)
.mutant-*
*.mutant-backup-*

# Control sidecars, same hazard from the other direction (STORY-33.10.01). TC-04's A/B needs a
# copy of `generate-dashboard.js` with the pre-ADR-0267 hardcoded output path restored, and that
# copy has to sit IN 93-Scripts/ so its `__dirname`-relative requires (lib/, the sibling modules,
# assets/) resolve identically — otherwise the two legs differ for reasons other than the line
# under test. Removed in `finally` and on SIGINT/SIGTERM, and swept at the start of each run; this
# is the belt for the case none of those fire. Unlike a mutant sidecar it is a WORKING copy, which
# is worse, not better: `lib/ship-filter.js` also excludes it, because a silent duplicate of a
# production script would otherwise be copied into every consumer install and into the public
# plugin, carrying no denylist token and so passing the scrub gate untouched.
.control-*

# EPIC-33 — the kit-side Preact board build workspace (ADR-0226 §1, ADR-0229).
# esbuild/preact/node_modules live HERE and nowhere else; the built runtime bundle is
# a regenerable output of `npm run board:build`, not a source file.
board/node_modules/
board/out/

# The staging deliverable of the ported board (STORY-33.1.01). ~30 MB and rebuilt on
# demand; cutover to the committed DASHBOARD.html name is STORY-33.9.05.
# MOVED 2026-08-27 -- the ported board now builds to board/dist/, which the `dist/` rule above
# already covers. This line is kept so a working tree that predates the move does not start
# tracking the stale copy it may still be carrying; acceptance-run.test.js reports that copy
# and asks for it to be deleted. Remove this line once no live tree has one.
_00-Project-Management/42-Monitor/DASHBOARD-NEXT.html
board/__redsrc/

# Design prototype, generated 2026-08-27 (10.4 MB: a self-contained redesign HTML plus the
# board payload it was extracted from). It was untracked, and a `git add -A` swept it into a
# commit it had nothing to do with. Nothing in the repo references this folder -- the PRD it
# relates to lives at 20-Requirements/CommandCenter/PRD-command-center-redesign.md. Ignored so
# the accident cannot repeat; delete this block if the prototype should be versioned.
command-center-redesign/

# Playwright home for the EPIC-34 board-UX compare specs (ADR-0274): tests/board-ux carries its
# own package.json + node_modules (already covered by the node_modules/ rule above). Dev-only,
# never shipped — board/ stays the build toolchain's (esbuild/preact) only home.
tests/board-ux/test-results/
tests/board-ux/playwright-report/

# STORY-33.9.05 assembly-lane interchange artefacts (review M2/M3): staging boards and
# payload hand-off files are per-run scratch, wherever they land.
*.assembling
*.payload.json
